---@class MakiUiBufOpts
---@field scratch? boolean Keep the buffer out of the live slot (for floats opened during a tool call). Default false.

---@class MakiSpanStyle
---@field fg? string `"#rrggbb"`, a terminal color name, or a palette index like `"4"`.
---@field bg? string Same forms as `fg`.
---@field bold? boolean
---@field italic? boolean
---@field underline? boolean
---@field dim? boolean
---@field strikethrough? boolean
---@field reversed? boolean

---@alias MakiLine string|table
-- A plain string, or a sequence of `{text, style?}` spans where `style` is a
-- named string (e.g. `"bold"`) or a `MakiSpanStyle` table.

---@class MakiUiBuf
-- Content buffer holding styled lines. The first buffer created in a task
-- becomes the "live" buffer streamed to the UI while the tool runs.
maki_ui_Buf = {}

---Append a single line to the end of the buffer.
---@param line MakiLine Plain string or sequence of `{text, style?}` spans.
function maki_ui_Buf:line(line) end

---Replace every line in the buffer (e.g. to redraw after a view toggle).
---@param lines MakiLine[] Sequence of line values, same format as `line()`.
function maki_ui_Buf:set_lines(lines) end

---Register an event handler. `"click"` fires when the user clicks a line
---(receives a click-event table, may yield/mutate); `"change"` fires
---synchronously after every mutation and must not yield. Re-registering an
---event replaces the previous handler.
---@param event "click"|"change" Event name.
---@param callback fun() Handler function.
function maki_ui_Buf:on(event, callback) end

---@class MakiOpenWinOpts
---@field width? integer|string Window width: absolute columns or `"N%"`. Default `"60%"`.
---@field height? integer|string Window height: absolute rows or `"N%"`. Default `"70%"`.
---@field row? integer Row offset from the anchor corner (negative moves up).
---@field col? integer Column offset from the anchor corner.
---@field anchor? string `"NW"` (default), `"NE"`, `"SW"`, `"SE"`, or `"input_caret"`.
---@field border? string `"rounded"` (default), `"single"`, `"double"`, `"none"`.
---@field title? string Text in the top border. Default `""`.
---@field title_pos? string `"left"` (default), `"center"`, `"right"`.
---@field footer? string[][] Key-hint `{key, label}` pairs in the bottom border.
---@field zindex? integer Stacking order. Default 50.
---@field cursor_line? boolean Highlight the focused row. Default false.
---@field reserved_top? integer Rows reserved at the top of the content area. Default 0.
---@field reserved_bottom? integer Rows reserved at the bottom of the content area. Default 0.
---@field split? string `"above"`, `"below"`, `"left"`, `"right"`, `"panel"`, or `""` (floating, default).
---@field order? integer Paint order among splits at the same edge. Default 50.
---@field focus? boolean Take keyboard focus on open. Default true.
---@field keys? string[] Keys (in `maki.keymap` notation) this window takes while on screen. Requires `focus = false`. `<C-c>`/`<C-z>` are refused.
---@field visible? boolean Initially visible. Default true.
---@field needs_input? boolean The window means the session needs user input. Default false.
---@field stack? boolean Floating only: offset past other stacked windows sharing the anchor. Default false.

---@class MakiWinConfig
-- Partial float config for `Win:set_config`; only included fields change.
---@field title? string Border title text.
---@field title_pos? string `"left"`, `"center"`, or `"right"`.
---@field footer? string[][] Key-hint `{key, label}` pairs in the bottom border.
---@field border? string `"rounded"`, `"single"`, `"double"`, or `"none"`.
---@field anchor? string `"NW"`, `"NE"`, `"SW"`, `"SE"`, or `"input_caret"`.
---@field width? integer|string New width; integer or `"N%"`.
---@field height? integer|string New height; integer or `"N%"`.
---@field zindex? integer Stacking order.
---@field cursor_line? boolean Highlight the focused row.
---@field reserved_top? integer Rows reserved at the top of the content area.
---@field split? string `"above"`, `"below"`, `"left"`, `"right"`, `"panel"`, or `""`.
---@field order? integer Paint order among split windows.
---@field needs_input? boolean The window means the session needs user input.

---@class MakiUiWin
-- Handle to a floating/split window from `maki.ui.open_win`.
---@field width integer Initial content width in columns.
---@field height integer Initial content height in rows.
---@field visible boolean Current visibility.
maki_ui_Win = {}

---Update the window layout on the fly; only included fields change.
---@param opts MakiWinConfig
function maki_ui_Win:set_config(opts) end

---Move the highlighted cursor line to `row` (1-indexed). Visible only when
---opened with `cursor_line = true`.
---@param row integer Target row, 1-indexed.
function maki_ui_Win:set_cursor(row) end

---Close the window and free its resources. Safe to call more than once.
function maki_ui_Win:close() end

---Hide the window without closing it (keeps state/buffer; takes no space,
---draws nothing, claims no keys). Bring back with `show()`.
---NOTE: `show()` itself is intentionally not stubbed here (focused surface only).
function maki_ui_Win:hide() end

---@class MakiChatInput
---@field session_id string Tab the value was read from (pass to `input_edit`).
---@field text string Whole value, newlines included.
---@field cursor integer Byte offset of the cursor into `text`.
---@field version integer Change counter (pass to `input_edit`).

---@class MakiUi
maki.ui = {}

---Create a new buffer for building UI content.
---@param opts? MakiUiBufOpts
---@return MakiUiBuf buf Buffer handle.
function maki.ui.buf(opts) end

---Show a short-lived message in the status bar. Without a UI, goes to the log.
---@param msg string Message text.
function maki.ui.flash(msg) end

---Run a built-in UI action by name, exactly as its default keybinding would.
---No action exists for sending the user's message.
---@param name MakiActionName Action name, e.g. `"file_picker"`.
---@return boolean|nil ok true on success, or nil plus an error.
---@return string|nil err Error for an unknown name or a missing UI.
function maki.ui.action(name) end

---Open a floating/split window displaying `buf`. No effect without a UI.
---@param buf MakiUiBuf Buffer to display.
---@param opts MakiOpenWinOpts Float configuration.
---@return MakiUiWin win Window handle.
function maki.ui.open_win(buf, opts) end

---Read the chat input text and cursor position. Offsets are byte offsets
---into `text` (newline counts as one byte).
---@return MakiChatInput|nil state The input state, or nil plus an error.
---@return string|nil err
function maki.ui.input() end

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 4. `maki.api`: plugin registration
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

---@class MakiToolCtx
-- Context passed as the second handler argument `(input, ctx)`.
maki_api_ToolCtx = {}

---"compact" when the result goes to the model, "full" when e.g.
---`code_execution` called. Apply output limits only in compact mode.
---@return "compact"|"full" mode
function maki_api_ToolCtx:output_mode() end

---@class MakiToolResultImage
---@field media_type string
---@field data string Base64 image data.

---@class MakiToolResult
---@field llm_output? string Result text for the model or calling code.
---@field is_error? boolean Treat the result as an error.
---@field header? string One-line header shown before the body.
---@field format? string `"plain"` (default) or `"markdown"`.
---@field annotation? string Short label shown next to the tool call.
---@field written_path? string Path of a file written by the tool.
---@field diff_path? string Path for a diff output block.
---@field diff_before? string Before text of the diff.
---@field diff_after? string After text of the diff.
---@field image? MakiToolResultImage `{media_type, data}` base64 image.
---@field state? any Serializable state forwarded to restore.
-- NOTE: `body`/`header` may also be Buf handles; typed as string here for focus.

---@class MakiToolSpec
---@field name string Required. ASCII identifier, up to 64 chars.
---@field description string Required. Non-empty; the model reads it to decide usage.
---@field schema table Required. JSON Schema object for the tool input.
---@field handler fun(input: table, ctx: MakiToolCtx): string|MakiToolResult Required. Returns a plain string or a richer output table.
---@field audiences? string[] Which model audiences see the tool. Default: all audiences.
---@field kind? string Grouping label (e.g. `"filesystem"`).
---@field timeout? number Execution timeout in seconds. 0/false disables; default inherits agent deadline.
---@field permission_scopes? string|fun(input: table): string[] Schema field (or function of input) returning path scopes needing write permission; declaring it puts the tool in front of the permission prompt.
---@field permission? string Required with `permission_scopes`: `"fs_read"`, `"fs_write"`, `"net"`, `"run"`, or `"env"`.
---@field mutable_path? string Schema string field for the primary written path. Required with `permission = "fs_write"`.
-- NOTE: `header`/`restore`/`start`/`describe` callbacks, `examples`, and
-- `start_annotation` are also documented but omitted here for focus.

---@class MakiCommandOpts
---@field args string Raw argument string (whitespace kept, may be empty).
---@field fargs string[] Args split into whitespace-separated words.

---@class MakiCommandSpec
---@field name string Required. Command name (leading `/` added when missing).
---@field description? string Short description shown in the command palette.
---@field nargs? 0|1|"?"|"*"|"+" How many args, like nvim's nargs. Default 0.
---@field handler fun(opts: MakiCommandOpts) Required. Called with `{args, fargs}`.

---@class MakiPromptHintSpec
---@field slot string Required. Aggregate slot name (e.g. `"tool_usage"`, `"general"`). Throws on singleton slots.
---@field content string|fun(): string Required. Static text or `function()` returning a string. Max 1 MiB.
---@field prompt? string|string[] Restrict to specific prompt ids (e.g. `"system"`).

---@class MakiSetPromptSpec
---@field slot string Required. Singleton slot name (e.g. `"identity"`, `"tone"`). Throws on aggregate slots.
---@field content string|fun(): string Required. Static text or `function()` returning a string. Max 1 MiB.
---@field prompt? string|string[] Restrict to specific prompt ids.

---@class MakiOptionSpec
---@field default? boolean|number|string Used when the user sets nothing; its Lua type becomes the option type.
---@field type? string Required when there is no default: `"boolean"`, `"integer"`, `"number"`, or `"string"`.
---@field min? number Minimum accepted value, numeric options only.
---@field desc string Required. One line shown in the configuration docs.

---@class MakiToolEntry
---@field name string
---@field schema table
---@field audiences string[]
---@field kind? string
---@field enabled? boolean Computed via `opts.config.disabled_tools` (get_tools only).
-- NOTE: `get_tool` entries for Lua-registered tools also carry wrapped
-- `header`/`restore` functions; omitted here for focus.

---@class MakiGetToolsOpts
---@field config? table Optional config with a `disabled_tools` string[] field used for each entry's `enabled` flag.

---@class MakiAutocmdOpts
---@field callback fun(ev: table) Called with `{id, event, match, data}`.
---@field once? boolean Remove the handler after it fires once. Default false.
---@field pattern? string|string[] Only fire on match. `"*"` matches everything; omit to match all.

---@class MakiExecAutocmdsOpts
---@field pattern? string Passed to callbacks as `ev.match`.
---@field data? any Arbitrary value passed as `ev.data`.

---@class MakiApi
maki.api = {}

---Register a tool the agent can call. Queued during plugin load, committed
---once the plugin finishes loading.
---@param spec MakiToolSpec
function maki.api.register_tool(spec) end

---Register a slash-command for the user input bar (`/name`).
---@param spec MakiCommandSpec
function maki.api.register_command(spec) end

---Append text to an aggregate prompt slot (concatenated with other plugins'
---contributions). A function `content` is called before every run.
---@param spec MakiPromptHintSpec
function maki.api.register_prompt_hint(spec) end

---Declare options under `plugins.<name>` in `maki.setup`; returns the user
---value merged with defaults. Call once at the top level of the plugin file.
---@param spec table<string, MakiOptionSpec> Map of option name to spec.
---@return table<string, boolean|number|string|nil> opts Merged options (nil where neither user value nor default exists).
function maki.api.register_options(spec) end

---Set a singleton prompt slot (replaces your plugin's previous value).
---A function `content` behaves as in `register_prompt_hint`.
---@param spec MakiSetPromptSpec
function maki.api.set_prompt(spec) end

---List all registered tools (static descriptions; describe callbacks not invoked).
---@param opts? MakiGetToolsOpts
---@return MakiToolEntry[] tools Array of `{name, schema, audiences, kind?, enabled}`.
function maki.api.get_tools(opts) end

---Look up a single tool by exact name.
---@param name string Exact tool name.
---@return MakiToolEntry|nil tool Metadata table, or nil if not found.
function maki.api.get_tool(name) end

---Run a slash command by name, as if typed (leading `/` optional; names
---match exactly apart from case). Returns once dispatched, not on completion.
---@param cmdline string Command line, e.g. `"/new"` or `"/cd ~/src"`.
---@return boolean|nil ok true once dispatched, or nil plus an error for unknown commands.
---@return string|nil err
function maki.api.run_command(cmdline) end

---Listen for one or more events. Jobs started inside a callback die with the
---dispatch unless awaited there or handed to a session.
---@param event MakiEventName|MakiEventName[] Event name or list of names.
---@param opts MakiAutocmdOpts
---@return integer id Autocmd id for `del_autocmd`.
function maki.api.create_autocmd(event, opts) end

---Remove a previously registered autocmd. No-op if `id` does not exist.
---@param id integer Id returned by `create_autocmd`.
function maki.api.del_autocmd(id) end

---Fire events manually; every matching callback runs to completion before
---this returns. A handler may suspend, so this call may too.
---@param event MakiEventName|MakiEventName[] Event name or list of names.
---@param opts? MakiExecAutocmdsOpts
function maki.api.exec_autocmds(event, opts) end

