---@class MakiSessionNotifyOpts
---@field session? string Id of a live session.
-- NOTE: the reference does not state a default session for `notify`
-- (unlike `set_mode`/`prompt`); pass `session` explicitly off the focused tab.
---@field wake? boolean Start a TUI turn when it next becomes idle. Default false.

---@class MakiSessionPromptOpts
---@field session? string Id of a live session; defaults to the focused one.

---@class MakiSessionModeOpts
---@field session? string Id of a live session; defaults to the focused one.

---@class MakiSession
maki.session = {}

---Report `text` to a live session without creating a user turn; the
---observation waits for the session's next agent run. Works everywhere, ACP included.
---@param text string What to report. Must not be blank.
---@param opts? MakiSessionNotifyOpts
---@return boolean|nil ok true, or nil plus an error.
---@return string|nil err
function maki.session.notify(text, opts) end

---Switch a live session between plan and build mode. Entering plan mode
---allocates the session's plan file if it has none.
---@param mode MakiSessionMode `"build"` or `"plan"`.
---@param opts? MakiSessionModeOpts
---@return boolean|nil ok true, or nil plus an error.
---@return string|nil err
function maki.session.set_mode(mode, opts) end

---Send `text` as a regular user prompt (never interpreted: slash commands,
---`exit`, `!` prefixes go to the model verbatim). Queued while streaming.
---@param text string The prompt to send. Must not be blank.
---@param opts? MakiSessionPromptOpts
---@return ("started"|"queued")|nil state `"started"` or `"queued"`, or nil plus an error.
---@return string|nil err
function maki.session.prompt(text, opts) end

