function maki.env.logs_dir() end

---Legacy config path (`~/.maki`) when it exists on disk (migration logic).
---@return string|nil dir Legacy directory path, or nil when absent.
function maki.env.legacy_dir() end

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 11. `maki.pack`
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

---@class MakiPackSpec
---@field src string Git source: any URI `git clone` accepts. The package name is derived from it (last segment, minus `.git`) unless `name` overrides it.
---@field name? string Directory/owner name override. Needed when two sources end in the same repository name.
---@field version? string Branch, tag, or commit to resolve. Follows the default branch when omitted. A recorded `pack-lock.json` revision wins over this.
---@field data? any Any Lua value, handed to a custom `load` function as `package.spec.data`.

---@class MakiPackPackage
-- Argument a custom `load` function receives. Runs as the package owner, so
-- `require()` inside it resolves in the package checkout.
---@field spec MakiPackSpec The spec (with `data`); `src` is credential-redacted.
---@field path? string Checkout directory the package loaded from.

---@class MakiPackAddOpts
---@field confirm? boolean Confirm new sources in the terminal before installing. Default true. Skips the install prompt only, never permission approval.
---@field load? boolean|fun(package: MakiPackPackage) `false` installs without loading at startup (activate later with `maki.packadd`); a function sets a custom entry point instead of `plugin/*.lua`. Default true.

---@class MakiPackRecord
---@field spec MakiPackSpec The declaration (plus lockfile state); `src` is credential-redacted.
---@field path? string Checkout directory, once installed.
---@field rev? string Recorded commit, once installed.
---@field active boolean Whether the package is active this session.

---@class MakiPack
-- `add` is only available in the global `init.lua`; `get` is read-only and
-- also available in project config and packages.
maki.pack = {}

---Declare global packages. Installs (clones) run after the global `init.lua`
---finishes; one unreachable repository is reported and skipped. Removing an
---entry stops loading it (lockfile entry + checkout linger until deleted).
---@param specs (string|MakiPackSpec)[] Sources or spec tables.
---@param opts? MakiPackAddOpts
function maki.pack.add(specs, opts) end

---Read package state without changing the installed set.
---@param names? string[] Package names; omit for all managed packages.
---@return MakiPackRecord[]|nil packages Records with `spec`, `path`, `rev`, `active`.
---@return string|nil err Error when the pack lockfile cannot be read.
function maki.pack.get(names) end

